###############################################################################
# 10. TRAINING MEMORY
#
# The first endpoint that reads what the user actually DID, rather than what
# they are. POST a session log, get back per-exercise performance records.
#
# `ExercisePerformanceRecord` is DERIVED data by design: recomputable from the
# log, cached only because "what can this user lift on this movement?" is asked
# on every prescription. So there is deliberately no way to hand one in -- the
# records are always rebuilt from the sessions in the request.
#
# The headline field is estimated_one_rep_max_kg, and it matters more than it
# looks: it is the reference that would make "heavy" mean something. Today the
# engine solves load from volume, which is why §7(d) has to warn that a 4x8@80
# bench becomes 4x4@160 under a strength objective. Nothing consumes e1RM yet
# -- that is M8b.
#
# THREE REFUSALS, all deliberate. Each returns null rather than a number:
#   - reps > 10        Epley and Brzycki are fitted on low-rep sets and diverge
#                      sharply beyond; a 20-rep set is endurance evidence
#   - load = 0         a bodyweight set has nothing to extrapolate from
#   - reps = 1         not a refusal but a special case: a completed single IS
#                      a 1RM, so it is returned as-is. Epley would otherwise
#                      report 103.3 for a measured 100kg single
#
# `as_of` is required rather than defaulted to now, because the rolling windows
# are measured back from it and reconstructing a past prescription must see the
# history as it stood then.
###############################################################################

### A four-session log covering every interesting case at once.
#
# bench: a warm-up set (60x20, must not count), two working sets at 8x80, an
#        older 5x85 and an older-still 10x70;
# squat: a single session at 5x120;
# push-up: bodyweight, unestimable;
# plus a SKIPPED session holding the heaviest bench in the file (8x90) -- it is
# adherence evidence, not strength evidence, and must not raise the estimate.
#
# Observed: exercises_with_estimate = 2, without = 1.
#   barbell-bench-press  e1RM 101.33 (Epley on 8x80 -- beats 5x85's 99.17 and
#                        10x70's 93.33; the skipped 8x90 that would have given
#                        114.0 is correctly absent). 3 sessions, 4 working sets
#                        (the warm-up is excluded), v7d 1280, v28d 2405,
#                        average_rpe 8.375
#   barbell-full-squat   e1RM 140.0, 1 session, v7d 600
#   push-up              e1RM null, formula null -- but the record still exists
#                        with 1 working set. Never-performed and
#                        performed-but-unestimable are different states
POST {{host}}/performance-records
Content-Type: application/json

