### (c) THE GUARD: the same three-day rhythm, but only five sessions logged.
#
# This is the request that matters most in this section. The ratio comes out at
# 2.40 -- higher than the genuine spike in (b) -- purely because the four-week
# window is mostly empty. That is the standard criticism of this metric, and it
# is why the state is "unknown" and load_multiplier is 1.0: a new user's second
# ordinary week must not be deloaded on arithmetic about weeks they had not
# started training in yet.
#
# Observed: state "unknown", ratio 2.40 reported anyway (the evidence travels
# with the refusal), load_multiplier 1.0, dose_outcome "varied".
POST {{host}}/vary
